.TH CWE-470 7 "2026-11-15" "CWE Top 25 (2025)" "Software Weakness Reference"
.SH NAME
CWE\-470 \- Use of Externally\-Controlled Input to Select Classes or Code (Unsafe Reflection)
.SH RANK
Appendix \- not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: Injection / Appendix (not in Top 25).
.SH DESCRIPTION
NOTE: CWE\-470 is NOT part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; it is included here as a related weakness for completeness.
.PP
Externally\-controlled input chooses which class is loaded or which method/code is invoked via reflection. An attacker who controls the name can instantiate unexpected classes or reach code paths that enable code execution, denial of service, or logic bypass. Closely related to CWE\-94 and CWE\-502.
.SH MITIGATION
Never let untrusted input name a class, method, or module directly. Map a small set of allowed identifiers to known types/handlers with an allow\-list, and reject anything else.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB2\fR exploited CVEs mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2021\-21985
VMware vCenter Server, added 2021\-11\-03, ransomware: Known.
.PP
VMware vCenter Server Improper Input Validation Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
VMware vSphere Client contains an improper input validation vulnerability in the Virtual SAN Health Check plug\-in, which is enabled by default in vCenter Server, which allows for remote code execution.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2021\-11\-17.
.PP
